{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Praise Him with the nevel, with the asor.</b> Rabbi Moses said: a nevel that has ten holes. And he did not speak correctly, for nevel is a instrument by itself, and likewise asor, as if he said: with a nevel, with an asor, in the manner of כרע כאח לי (like a brother to me). And similar to it: ככבש אלוף — like ככבש כאלוף, for the kaf serves on behalf of two, in the manner of the bet in אל שדי יעשה חפצו. And the proof that they are two: עלי עשור ועלי נבל."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:29:15.646784685Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}